Patch 32 -- deduplicate fixed-function shaders by exact generated GLSL source.

The normal WineD3D FFP caches use the complete D3D settings structures as
keys. On the corrected save-load route those keys produced 36 stage programs
from only 19 byte-distinct GLSL sources. The 17 duplicate links cost 2.04 s on
the RG353VS. This patch keeps the settings descriptors but makes their GL
shader and separable-stage owner canonical by source.

The 64-bit FNV-1a hash is only a rejection filter. Equality requires matching
length and a full memcmp, so a hash collision cannot merge different shaders.
The shared owner is destroyed after both settings trees, avoiding double
deletion and keeping all program/pipeline users alive through teardown.

MGS2_GL_SOURCE_DEDUP=0 disables reuse for a device A/B. The bounded GPU probe
also records source hash and size in compile_shader events; it performs no I/O.

Measured 2026-08-13, fixed 1,992 MHz, one instance, corrected autoload route
(default walk direction down):
  cache off: 36 compile/stage events; 17 exact duplicates; duplicate links
             2,036,500 us (4 vertex / 13 fragment)
  cache on:  22 compile/stage events; 0 exact duplicates
Both post-load screenshots were correct and contained the first guard.

